///1XSUB
Help by Willem Aandewiel
XSUB - Extend SUBMIT with program input

///2USAGE
Put XSUB on the first line of a .SUB file.
Subsequent lines can also be supplied to programs using buffered
console input through BDOS function 10.

///2EXAMPLE
A simple DDT test:

  XSUB
  DDT
  X
  G0

Save this as TRY.SUB and run SUBMIT TRY in a suitable writable
batch environment. DDT displays registers and then exits.

///2LIMITS
XSUB does not support every program or every kind of keyboard input.
Single-character input and custom keyboard routines are not covered.
A warm start may display (xsub active); XSUB is still resident.
A cold restart removes it from memory.
SUBMIT's disk requirements still apply.
